    // - Specifically:
    //   - 4! = 24, and 2! * 2! * 3! = 2 * 2 * 6 = 24. So one 4 can become 3,2,2 (three digits instead of one)
    //   - 6! = 720, and 5! * 3! = 120 * 6 = 720. So one 6 can become 5,3 (two digits instead of one)
    //   - 8! = 40320, and 7! * 2! = 5040 * 2 = 10080, no. 8! = 2^7 * 3^2 * 5 * 7. 
